            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0043" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.939/247: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-16T12:00:00+09:00">August 16,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 16—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>535. Department’s 281, August 11, 7 p.m., via Peiping, hides and skins embargo.
                    In view of the information given in Tientsin’s 154, August 10, 3 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d56-f1"/> and 155, August 15, noon, we propose to take no
                    further action unless Tientsin finds that the modification of the embargo fails
                    satisfactorily to alleviate the restriction on American exporters.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
